<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estonian Declaration of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Manifesto to the Peoples of Estonia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Estonian Declaration of Independence, formally the Manifesto to the Peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, was issued by the Salvation Committee and proclaimed in Pärnu on 23 February and in Tallinn on 24 February 1918, between the Bolshevik withdrawal and the German occupation. It declared Estonia an independent democratic republic, and 24 February is celebrated as Independence Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/estonian-declaration-of-independence.jpg" alt="Estonian Declaration of Independence" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Declaration_of_Estonian_independence_in_P%C3%A4rnu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
